<title>USA: Atlanta approves $213 million Hawks arena.</title>
<headline>Atlanta approves $213 million Hawks arena.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlanta City Council approved a $213 million basketball arena near Centennial Olympic Park, city officials said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The council approved the plan 13-0 Monday. It still needs approval from Fulton County Commission, which will consider the plan Wednesday.</p>
<p>Turner Broadcasting System Inc plans to build the arena for the Atlanta Hawks and possibly a National Hockey League expansion team.</p>
<p>The plan calls for the arena to be financed with taxable bonds, while $72 million of tax-exempt bonds would be issued to fund public improvements  around the facility.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
